.Ruserdata

# Example code in package build process
*-Ex.R

# Output files from R CMD build
/*.tar.gz

# Output files from R CMD check
/*.Rcheck/

# RStudio files
.Rproj.user/

# produced vignettes
vignettes/*.html
vignettes/*.pdf

# OAuth2 token, see https://github.com/hadley/httr/releases/tag/v0.3
.httr-oauth

# knitr and R markdown default cache directories
*_cache/
/cache/

# Temporary files created by R markdown
*.utf8.md
*.knit.md

# R Environment Variables
.Renviron

# Secrets and local deployment credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
.wrangler/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519
credentials.json
secrets.json

# renv library
renv/library/
renv/staging/

# jamovi options js
jamovi/ui/*.options.js

# packaged module
*.jmo

# build folders
build/
build*/

# ...but buildres/ holds the Electron packaging icon, which is a source
# asset: without it a fresh clone cannot package the desktop app. Git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so the
# directory itself has to be un-excluded first.
!standalone/electron/buildres/
!standalone/electron/buildres/**

# other files / folders
temp/
man/
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log
inst/doc
tests/testthat/Rplots.pdf

# backup/temp files
*.backup
*.current
*.new
*.broken

# duplicate color reference at root
/color-reference.html
inst/tools/

# self-referencing symlink
/plotstudio
/pandion

# tooling / scratch / build artifacts (machine-specific)
.claude/
.codex_backups/
.plan.md
.zip
build.log
build_verbose.log
jmo_extracted/
backup_*/

# Minified widget JS: COMMITTED since v2.9.5 (was gitignored). A plain
# `jmc --build` on a fresh clone must produce a working module - without
# min.js the runtime falls back to inlining the ~6 MB source, which can
# freeze the results webview (the v2.4.1 regression; re-hit by a
# jamovi-team from-source build, Jul 2026). The Stop hook + release.sh
# + CI keep it fresh; R/widget.R's hash check refuses a stale copy.

# Shipped user guide (generated from docs/ by scripts/jmv-build-install.sh
# and the CI workflow; docs/ is the canonical copy)
inst/docs/

# Local architecture/codebase diagrams (kept out of release history)
docs/diagrams/

# distribution output (jamovi team builds these; never committed)
dist/

# personal dev docs -- kept locally, not distributed publicly
/LAUNCH-QA-CHECKLIST*.html
/PLOT_STUDIO_BACKLOG.md
/PANDION_BACKLOG.md
/docs/tab-mapping-spec.md

# dev-only: project instructions + prototypes/experiments (kept local, not public)
/CLAUDE.md
/prototypes/

# reference copies of upstream source dropped in for local study (jmv /
# jamovi app code) - NEVER commit into this repo (AGPL upstream + bloat;
# release.sh stages with `git add -A`, so this guard is load-bearing)
/Jamovi Source Files/
/Jamovi Source Code/

# Local review artifact: regenerate with website/build-preview.py
website/pandion-site-preview.html

# Superseded brand art parked by the t4-13 tidy-up (11 MB of PNGs that were
# never committed; release.sh stages with `git add -A`, so without this guard
# they would ride into git history permanently). rm -rf the folder itself to
# make the removal permanent; website/assets/ is the source of truth.
/branding/superseded/

# Local design explorations. This tree includes an independent nested Git
# repository, generated deployment state, and node_modules; it is not part of
# the Pandion source or release.
/mockups/

# Standalone build output is reproduced by standalone/build-dist.sh and is
# attached by the release workflow. Scratch probes are local investigations;
# the maintained verification suite lives in standalone/verify/.
/standalone/dist/
/scratchpad/
/standalone/scratchpad/

# Prepared release bundles are reproducible local/CI outputs. The committed
# sources and generated website artifacts remain the release source of truth.
/.release/

# Internal working material stays LOCAL (Torry, Aug 20 2026). This repo is
# public, and correspondence, audits and working notes are not things a user
# or contributor needs to build or run the app - while they do quote named
# third parties and colleagues verbatim. The line: the repo carries code,
# README, licence, the shipped user guide, the website and the release
# checklists; everything that is correspondence, internal critique or a
# working note lives on disk only, like CLAUDE.md already does.
#
# These were previously tracked and remain in git HISTORY - untracking stops
# further exposure, it does not erase the past. Scrubbing history was
# considered and deliberately declined: it renames every commit since July
# 2026, strands other clones and worktrees, and still leaves copies GitHub
# must be asked to purge.
/docs/jonathon-svg-findings.md
/planning/
/GHOST-TOGGLE-FIX-PROPOSAL.md
/ROTATE-TEXT-BOX-NOTE.md

# Local review and handoff artifacts.
/COPY-FIX-HANDOFF-v*.md
/PANDION-RENAME-PLAN.md
/PANDION-RENAME-QA.html
/PANDION-STANDALONE-LAUNCH-CHECKLIST.html
/RELEASE-QA-v*.html
/RESULTS-ROLL-DIAGNOSIS.md
